WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:11.910
Hey Wisecrack, Jared here and today we’re
taking a fresh look at the 1995 classic that

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:17.789
seamlessly combined mind-bending metaphysical
themes and cartoon boobs- Ghost in the Shell.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:21.929
Yeah, we know there’s a new version out,
but apparently they forgot to put in a lot

00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:25.699
of the brainy stuff so we decided to talk
about the original.

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:29.350
Many have weighed in over the years on what
the film says about the line between human

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.480
and machine but that’s not what we’re
talking about today.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.690
Instead, we’re going to examine the film’s
warning about humanity’s potentially fatal

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.570
flaw and its roadmap for a more evolved civilization.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.760
Ghost in the Shell is probably one of the
most philosophicaly complex animated films

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.420
out there, so a big shout out to Naruto Online
for sponsoring this video and supporting us

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.820
as we tackle this cultural milestone.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.770
Since some of the philosophy we’ll be covering
can get a bit confusing, stick around til

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:59.320
the end to hear us explain a key lesson using
the world of Naruto.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.050
Welcome to this Wisecrack Edition on The Philosophy
of Ghost in the Shell.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.579
And as always, spoilers ahead.

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:08.600
Ghost in the Shell had a huge impact on sci-fi.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.650
Works such as Ex Machina,The Matrix, and Westworld
echo not only the film’s aesthetics but

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.819
also the theme of mankind vs. technology.

00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:21.950
We often see this as a warning that technology
will take over and/or alter humanity for the

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:22.950
worse.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.969
I’m not talking about clickbait or selfies.

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:26.800
I’m talking about this.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.020
And this.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.180
You know, classic robot overlord stuff.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.850
However, Ghost in the Shell is different.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.929
While it’s set up to be a typical battle
between man and his creation, the resolution

00:01:41.929 --> 00:01:46.759
is not one side triumphing over the other,
but a synthesis between the two.

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:47.759
Don’t remember?

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:49.779
Can’t blame you - it’s probably been awhile.

00:01:49.779 --> 00:01:51.459
Here’s a quick refresher.

00:01:51.459 --> 00:01:56.810
The film centers around Major Motoko Kusanagi,a
cyborg government agent working for Section

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.380
9 - basically a black ops unit.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.409
Section 9 pursues a mysterious entity known
as the Puppet Master, who employs ghost-hacking

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:08.200
to monkey around with people’s memories and force
them to do its bidding.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:21.400
This super-hacker turns out to be a spy program
originally called Project 2501, which was

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.500
secretly developed by Section 6.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.740
They’re an intelligence division - sort
of like the CIA.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:31.319
Section 6 lost control of their creation after
it spontaneously developed self-awareness

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:34.230
by swimming in the vast ocean of the digital
world.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:40.500
When Kusanagi finally catches up to the Puppet
Master, it makes a rather forward proposal:

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.060
they should merge consciousnesses and create
a new, unique being.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:51.620
She accepts, and the film ends with the new
entity - call it the Kusanuppet Master - contemplating

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.879
what to do next.

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:54.090
Maybe a vacation?

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:59.120
The confrontation and resolution of these
two forces - human and digital consciousnesses

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:05.829
- reflects German philosopher Georg Hegel’s
vision of progress.

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:09.049
To Hegel, conflict progresses human history.

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:13.380
Every development, from the time of our illustrious
forefathers to the present day, is caused

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.629
by forces that clash and create something
new.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.250
This is Hegel’s “dialectics” in a nutshell.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.079
But before we get into that, we need to show
how Hegel’s fundamental ideas help build

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:25.300
the setting of Ghost in the Shell.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.859
First and foremost, Hegel’s philosophy is
driven by the belief that the world operates

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.780
on rational principles and that the true nature
of reality is knowable.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.499
Kusanagi is defined by this philosophical
idealism.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.500
She is driven by dissatisfaction with her
limited perspective,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.680
and is convinced that there is

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.360
a more perfect reality available to her.

00:03:49.379 --> 00:03:54.450
As such, the film treats the marriage of Kusanagi’s
human consciousness and the Puppet Master’s

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:59.680
artificial nature with a certain optimism,
and Hegel’s system of dialectics explains

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.180
why.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.440
But first, I want to distinguish Hegel’s
dialectics from the way the term is more commonly

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:05.450
understood.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.959
In classical philosophy, dialectics are a
form of argumentative discourse designed to

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:14.310
ferret out contradictions and arrive at a
better understanding of truth.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.709
You start with an argument, called a thesis,
which is met by a counter-argument called

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:19.989
an anti-thesis.

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:24.699
The end result may be a refutation of the
original proposition, an affirmation of the

00:04:24.699 --> 00:04:29.090
counter-argument, or a synthesis of the assertions
that results in a better understanding of

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.090
the subject.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:33.430
Think Socratic Method, or a lawyer cross-examining
a witness.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.569
The purpose is to learn the truth.

00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:39.870
In Hegel’s system, dialectics is more than
just philosophical inquiry - they are the

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:45.430
very mechanism by which humans progress, both
on an individual level and as a collective.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.900
When one force confronts another force, something
new ultimately emerges.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:53.949
At the heart of the film is a dialectic of
the human and digital worlds.

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:57.090
In one corner, we have Kusanagi and her human
mind.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:01.979
Her various memories and experiences combine
to make her a unique individual.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.540
And yet she feels constrained by her own limited
personal identity.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.460
In the other corner we have the Puppet Master,
who sprang forth from the vast informational

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:30.539
resources of cyber-reality and therefore possesses
the broader understanding that Kusanagi seeks.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.680
But the Puppet Master too feels limited, by
its lack of personal identity.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.960
In short, each has what the other needs.

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:58.280
Other films have us trained to think that
when technology gets a little too big for

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.590
its britches it need to be put in its place
so humanity can be preserved.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.610
But through the lens of Hegel's master/slave
dialectic, this meeting of the minds should

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.819
have no winner.

00:06:07.819 --> 00:06:12.620
Imagine a feudal lord of the middle ages and
the serfs bound to work his fields.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:17.389
The lord is the master - he can force the
serfs to toil away because he controls all

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:18.860
the agriculture in the area.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:22.919
The serfs are his slaves - peasants who can't
afford land of their own.

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:27.409
They work their asses off while the lord sits
back with a refreshing drink.

00:06:27.409 --> 00:06:29.150
Sounds great for the lord, right?

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:34.490
The problem is, as the serfs labor they get
better and better at farming, while the master

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.790
learns nothing new.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:40.270
He stagnates, while the serfs become more
powerful due to their valuable knowledge.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.700
This, according to Hegel, is what leads the
oppressed to overcome their masters.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:49.280
Still not making sense? Well, stick around till the end to hear it explained in the context of Naruto.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:54.340
Examples of oppressive masters and usurping
slaves resonate throughout Ghost in the Shell.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:04.080
Section 6, ostensibly pulling the Puppet Master’s
strings, remains antiquated, stagnant, and

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.500
stuck in the politics of the old world.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:16.200
They preserve some power through their mastery
of Project 2501, but gain nothing while the

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.660
Puppet Master slowly gains sentience as it
labors for them.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:24.540
Separately, the Puppet Master acts as master
when it uses its ghost-hacking ability to

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.600
hijack others and force them to do its bidding.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:32.340
We see this early in the film when Section
9 interrogates the garbageman and learns that

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:37.220
he was brainwashed into believing he was spying
on his wife, when in fact he was merely the

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.400
Puppet Master’s tool.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.600
But the Puppet Master's efforts are constantly thwarted

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.200
and it remains unable to escape the terms of its bondage.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:52.400
Similarly, Section 9’s typical M.O. is classic
“master” behavior; they use lethal force

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.440
to accomplish their goals, leaving no room
for compromise.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.580
The first time we see Batou, he’s bragging
that Section 9 has the authority to kill.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.020
And Aramaki’s approach to the Puppet Master
is to destroy it if Kusanagi can’t secure it.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.500
Ultimately, none of this is productive.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:17.160
It just makes it harder for Section 9 to understand
the Puppet Master’s true nature and prolongs

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.800
Kusanagi’s journey to enlightenment.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:24.660
The preferred result when two opposing forces
clash is synthesis, which Hegel refers to

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:25.740
as sublation.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:30.400
He means something very specific: it’s combination
without loss.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:35.940
The result is a unique, superior idea that
incorporates and accommodates both perspectives.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:40.760
That’s what the Puppet Master is proposing
when he suggests that he and Kusanagi merge.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.240
A cyborg is a great example of this.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.940
A cyborg is neither wholly man or machine.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:54.880
It’s a synthesis of man and machine - encompassing
both, it becomes something new.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.820
Sublation is crucial because it helps avoid
the stagnation that occurs when a person,

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.440
idea, or whatever becomes too insulated.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.520
Looking at Section 9, we see that the team
was composed with dialectical principles in mind.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:14.560
When Togusa asks Kusanagi why he, a non-augmented
human, is included on the team of cyborg bad-asses,

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.780
Kusanagi explains that his uniqueness makes
the group stronger.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:38.140
The Puppet Master too is aware of the problem
of stagnation, and that’s why he needs the

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.900
constraints that Kusanagi feels fettered by.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:05.660
This 
is reminiscent of a species from another classic

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.920
series - The Borg, from Star Trek.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:12.180
The Borg are an awesome villain and I’d
use any excuse to bring them up, but they

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.840
actually illustrate what we’re talking about
pretty well.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:19.640
The Borg is a cybernetic race that travels
the galaxy assimilating other species into

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:20.780
a collective mind.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:21.760
Why do they do this?

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:31.540
It’s the same reason.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.960
Without diversity, the weaknesses of the race
will inbreed and compound, rendering their

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.140
civilization vulnerable.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.640
Obviously, from the perspective of the assimilated,
there's some loss.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:45.960
The Borg get your smarts and fresh genetic
material, and all you get is a new, modern look.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:49.700
But from the perspective of the Borg, it's
a story of developing consciousness.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:56.400
Sublation is the climax of Ghost in the Shell
- not a battle to the death, but rather a

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.000
synthesis that results in a stronger, more
evolved being.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:10.640
For Hegel, the progress of human history happens
through conflicts like these, both on an individual

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.800
level and on a much larger scale.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:17.920
Everytime we make any kind of advance through
these dialectics, be it in science, art, or

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:22.240
what have you, the world enters a new state
of affairs that should represent an improvement

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.640
over what came before.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.760
Hegel calls this new state ‘geist.”

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:31.040
The word can be translated as “mind,”
“spirit,” or even...wait for it, “ghost.”

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:32.020
Soo..

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.480
Geist in the shell, anyone?

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.440
At the end of the film, after Kusanagi and
the Puppet Master have merged, we have a new

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:41.340
state of affairs in which this new type of
being exists.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.440
Call it a new era, call it evolution, call
it what you will - it’s geist, following

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:48.340
its trajectory towards an improved world.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:52.960
The film hints at this in the climactic battle
scene, when tank-fire obliterates the names

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:57.520
of less evolved creatures in the Tree of Life,
stopping at the top on “hominis.”

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:01.680
This symbolizes that evolution must continue
even past human beings.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:06.300
This is why Ghost in the Shell’s message
is so unique from other films in the genre.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:10.020
It’s not about what will happen
if we do merge with our technology, it’s

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.600
what will happen if we don’t.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.900
The message is to interact with the world,
resolve our contradictions with it, and emerge

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.760
stronger than we were before.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:21.600
Clinging to our beliefs about what we are
will only prevent us from becoming what we

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:22.720
can be.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:38.800
Put another way, “resistance is futile”
may sound bad coming from the Borg, but according

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:42.620
to Hegel, sublation is a necessary towards
progress.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.400
So it just may be true.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.240
Hey guys thanks for watching.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:51.340
Still a bit confused about Hegel’s Master/Slave
dialectic?

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.480
I don’t blame you.

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.220
Hegel is pretty freakin difficult.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:58.080
But luckily, if you’re a fan of Naruto,
I’ve got another way to explain it.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.660
Keep in mind, this scenario is entirely hypothetical.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.140
Let’s start at the beginning.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:06.960
Naruto desperately wants recognition from
the people of The Hidden Leaf Village by becoming

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:10.060
Hokage, or the master ninja of the village.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:15.480
Let’s say that Naruto uses sweet Jutsus
and the nine tailed fox spirit to FORCE people

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.900
to make him Hokage.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:22.040
By coercing the villagers to submit to him,
Naruto has gained mastery over them.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:26.100
In Hegel’s terms they will have become Naruto’s
slaves or bondsmen.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:30.780
Well, the problem is...just because he’s
now Hokage, that doesn’t mean he actually

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.980
has the skills.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:35.880
That doesn’t occur until hundreds of episodes
later after he defeats Pain.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:40.120
In fact, at this point, the villagers would
have no choice but to to do the bulk of the

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:44.900
protecting and ninja duties while Naruto just
sits back and takes all the credit.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:49.660
In other words, if the people are having to
fight invaders, build defenses, and craft

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:54.580
weapons, then THEY are the ones gaining the
skills becoming of sweet sweet Hokage-ness.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:14:00.040
Essentially, Naruto will never get any better
at being a Hokage, while his “subordinates”

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:03.140
are becoming more and more skilled at the
art of defense.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:08.600
So even though, in this hypothetical situation,
Naruto would be the Hokage, his claim to mastery

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:13.400
is slowly dissipating as the villagers come
to master the skills that supposedly define

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.460
his role as Hokage.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.000
So who’s the master and who's the slave?

